x = "" is a prefix match that is true for every string
(diag.equals_empty_string, warning, on the comparison), for all three
quote styles and on array elements. A string literal operand of = is
also diag.equals_vs_strict_equals (info tier).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Blank;
	:PARAMETERS sStatus, aRow;
	:DECLARE bBlank;
	:IF sStatus = "";
		sStatus := "Logged";
	:ENDIF;
	bBlank := aRow[2] = '' .OR. aRow[3] = [];
	:RETURN bBlank;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Blank;
	:PARAMETERS sStatus, aRow;
	:DECLARE bBlank;
	:IF sStatus = "";
		sStatus := "Logged";
	:ENDIF;
	bBlank := aRow[2] = '' .OR. aRow[3] = [];
	:RETURN bBlank;
:ENDPROC;
